⚡🇩🇪🇳🇱🇦🇹🇩🇰🇬🇷🇺🇬According to information cited by the Greek press, Germany, Austria, the Netherlands, Denmark, and Greece are finalizing a plan to build a repatriation center in Uganda, where migrants in irregular situations would be sent.

The facility is expected to have a capacity of between 5,000 and 10,000 people and is scheduled to be completed by 2027. The center would be primarily intended for "migrants who have caused problems in the countries where they are currently being hosted." Minors would be excluded from this mechanism.

